From 4e9510221bb5a4956250a153b65ab2a7397dce95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:16:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 032/113] drm/msm/adreno: base the TTBR1 global vm in the
 sign-extendable half

The GPU issues 48-bit VAs. Within the forced-TTBR1 aperture
(0xffff000000000000-0xffffffffffffffff on msm8998) the SMMU rebuilds
the full VA by sign-extending the top bit of the upstream address, so
the only TTBR1 addresses a 48-bit master can form are those with bit
47 set: 0xffff800000000000 and up. The previous fix left the vm based
at the aperture start, in the unreachable lower half -- every global
buffer was issued with bit 47 clear, sign-extended to a LOW address,
looked up in TTBR0 where nothing maps, and write-faulted.

This is what made GPU recovery fatal: the crashdumper allocates its
scratch in this vm, so recovery (or merely reading debugfs/dri/0/gpu)
faulted itself, a5xx_hw_init() failed with -22, and the device looped
until the bootloader gave up the slot.

Base the vm at 0xffff800000000000 with the size clamped so
start + size does not wrap u64 (a wrapped range makes every drm_mm
allocation fail with -ENOSPC and takes all of msm down).

Verified on taimen (against the pre-drm_gpuvm code this function has
since become): vm maps at 0xffff800000001000, reading
debugfs/dri/0/gpu (previously a deterministic wedge) returns state
cleanly, and a real runtime fault now goes fault -> hangcheck ->
recover -> GPU healthy again, with the session surviving.

Ported from taimen-v6.0 onto 6.18's adreno_iommu_create_vm(); the fix
itself carries over unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.c
index 61f67eef3682..af1041c74287 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.c
@@ -239,6 +239,30 @@ adreno_iommu_create_vm(struct msm_gpu *gpu,
 	if (start + size < start)
 		size = U64_MAX - start;
 
+	/*
+	 * The GPU issues 48-bit VAs. Within the TTBR1 aperture the SMMU
+	 * reconstructs the full 64-bit VA by sign-extending the top bit of the
+	 * upstream address (SEP), so the only TTBR1 VAs a 48-bit master can
+	 * actually form are the ones whose bit 47 is set:
+	 * 0xffff800000000000 and up. The aperture's lower half
+	 * (0xffff000000000000..0xffff7fffffffffff) is unreachable -- a buffer
+	 * placed there is issued with bit 47 clear, sign-extends to a LOW
+	 * address, gets looked up in TTBR0 where nothing maps it, and faults.
+	 *
+	 * That unreachable half is exactly where this vm used to start, and is
+	 * why running the crashdumper (GPU recovery, or any read of
+	 * debugfs/dri/0/gpu, which allocates its 1 MB scratch here) reliably
+	 * wedged the A540: the recovery path itself faulted, a5xx_hw_init()
+	 * returned -22, and the device looped to fastboot.
+	 *
+	 * Base the vm in the reachable half. The clamp above already keeps
+	 * start + size from wrapping.
+	 */
+	if (start == 0xffff000000000000ULL) {
+		start = 0xffff800000000000ULL;
+		size = U64_MAX - start;
+	}
+
 	DRM_DEV_INFO(&pdev->dev,
 		     "gpu aspace: aperture %#llx-%#llx, base %#llx, size %#llx\n",
 		     geometry->aperture_start, geometry->aperture_end,
